    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This page covers how to create lists that have complex list items."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "complex list item"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a list item that contains block content that follows the principal text (which may be empty). This is different from a list item whose principal text spans multiple lines, for which this page draws a distinction. The page goes on to explain how to attach a block to a list item in an ancestor list."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The main focus of the syntax covered on this page is to keep the list continuous (i.e., to prevent the list from breaking)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As with regular paragraph text, the principal text in a list item can span any number of lines as long as those lines are contiguous (i.e., adjacent with no empty lines). Multiple lines are combined into a single paragraph and wrap as regular paragraph text. This behavior holds even if the lines are indented, as shown in the third bullet in this example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* The document header in AsciiDoc is optional.\nIf present, it must start with a document title.\n\n* Optional author and revision information lines\nimmediately follow the document title.\n\n* The document header must be separated from\n  the remainder of the document by one or more\n  empty lines and it cannot contain empty lines."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The document header in AsciiDoc is optional. If present, it must start with a document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Optional author and revision information lines immediately follow the document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The document header must be separated from the remainder of the document by one or more empty lines and it cannot contain empty lines."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When list items contain more than one line of text, leave an empty line between items to make the list easier to read while working in the code. An empty line between two list items will not break the list."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Empty lines between two items in a list (ordered or unordered) will not break the list. For ordered lists, this means the numbering will be continuous rather than restarting at 1. (See "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "separating.html"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "separating.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " to learn how to force two adjacent lists apart)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If an empty line after a list item is followed by the start of a block, such as a paragraph or delimited block rather than another list item, the list will terminate at this point. If this happens, you’ll notice that a subsequent list item will be placed into a new list. For ordered lists, that means the numbering will restart (at 1)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "To keep the list continuous in those cases—​such as when you’re documenting complex steps in a procedure—​you must use a "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "list continuation"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "#list-continuation"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " to attach blocks to the list item. For ordered lists, this will ensure that the numbering continues from one list item to the next rather than being reset."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "_empty_lines_in_a_list",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Empty lines in a list"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_multiline_principal_text",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Multiline principal text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In addition to the principal text, a list item may contain block elements, including paragraphs, delimited blocks, and block macros. To add block elements to a list item, you must “attach” them (in a series) using a list continuation. A "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "list continuation"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "+"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " symbol on a line by itself, immediately adjacent to the block being attached."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "+"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " at the end of a line, rather than on a line by itself, is not a list continuation. Instead, it creates a hard line break."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of a list item that uses a list continuation:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title.\n+\nThe header is optional."
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
                        "context": "paragraph",
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "The header is optional."
                          }
                        ],
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Using a list continuation, you can attach any number of block elements to a list item. Unless the block is inside a delimited block which itself has been attached, each block must be preceded by a list continuation to form a chain of blocks."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example that attaches both a listing block and an admonition paragraph to the first list item:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title.\n+\n----\n= Document Title\n----\n+\nKeep in mind that the header is optional.\n\n* Optional author and revision information lines immediately follow the document title.\n+\n----\n= Document Title\nDoc Writer <doc.writer@asciidoc.org>\nv1.0, 2022-01-01\n----"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how the source is rendered:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
                        "context": "listing",
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "= Document Title"
                          }
                        ],
                        "language": "asciidoc",
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      },
                      {
                        "context": "paragraph",
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "Keep in mind that the header is optional."
                          }
                        ],
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
                        "context": "listing",
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "= Document Title\nDoc Writer <doc.writer@asciidoc.org>\nv1.0, 2022-01-01"
                          }
                        ],
                        "language": "asciidoc",
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "Optional author and revision information lines immediately follow the document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A list with complex content"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you’re attaching more than one block to a list item, you’re strongly encouraged to wrap the content inside an open block. That way, you only need a single list continuation line to attach the open block to the list item. Within the open block, you write like you normally would, no longer having to worry about adding list continuations between the blocks to keep them attached to the list item."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of wrapping complex list content in an open block:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title.\n+\n--\nHere's an example of a document title:\n\n----\n= Document Title\n----\n\nNOTE: The header is optional.\n--"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how that content is rendered:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "ulist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
                        "blocks": [
                          {
                            "context": "paragraph",
                            "id": null,
                            "inlines": [
                              {
                                "kind": "text",
                                "value": "Here’s an example of a document title:"
                              }
                            ],
                            "roles": [],
                            "title": null
                          },
                          {
                            "context": "listing",
                            "id": null,
                            "inlines": [
                              {
                                "kind": "text",
                                "value": "= Document Title"
                              }
                            ],
                            "language": "asciidoc",
                            "roles": [],
                            "title": null
                          },
                          {
                            "context": "admonition",
                            "id": null,
                            "inlines": [
                              {
                                "kind": "text",
                                "value": "The header is optional."
                              }
                            ],
                            "roles": [],
                            "title": null,
                            "type": "note"
                          }
                        ],
                        "context": "open",
                        "id": null,
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "The header in AsciiDoc must start with a document title."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "style": null,
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A list with complex content wrapped in an open block"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The open block wrapper is also useful if you’re including content from a shared file into a list item. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "* list item\n+\n--\ninclude::shared-content.adoc[]\n--"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By wrapping the include directive in an open block, the content can be used unmodified."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The only limitation of this technique is that the content itself may not contain an open block since open blocks cannot (yet) be nested."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "list-continuation",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Attach blocks using a list continuation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the principal text of a list item is empty, the node for the principal text is dropped. This is how you can get the first block (such as a listing block) to line up with the list marker. You can make the principal text empty by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "{empty}"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute reference."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s an example of a list that has items with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "only"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " complex content."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". {empty}\n+\n----\nprint(\"one\")\n----\n. {empty}\n+\n----\nprint(\"one\")\n----"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how the source is rendered:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "olist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "blocks": [
                      {
                        "context": "listing",
                        "id": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "print(\"one\")"
                          }
                        ],
                        "language": "asciidoc",
                        "roles": [],
                        "title": null
                      }
                    ],
                    "checkbox": null,
                    "inlines": []
                  },
                  {
