                        ],
                        "checkbox": null,
                        "inlines": [
                          {
                            "kind": "text",
                            "value": "grandparent list item"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ],
                    "roles": [],
                    "style": null,
                    "title": null
                  }
                ],
                "context": "example",
                "id": null,
                "roles": [],
                "title": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "A nested list enclosed in an open block"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The main limitation of this approach is that it can only be used once in the hierarchy (i.e., it can only enclose a single nested list). That’s because the open block itself cannot be nested. If you require more control, then you must use the ancestor list continuation."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "_enclose_in_open_block",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Enclose in open block"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Normally, a list continuation will attach a block to the current list item. For each empty line you add before the list continuation, the association will move up one level in the nesting. In other words, an empty line signals to the list continuation to back out of the current list by one level. As a result, the block will be attached to the current item in an ancestor list. This syntax is referred to as an "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "ancestor list continuation"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": [
                      "term"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "admonition",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The ancestor list continuation is a fragile syntax. For one, it may not be apparent to new authors that the empty lines before the list continuation are significant. That’s because the AsciiDoc syntax generally ignores repeating empty lines. There are also scenarios where even these empty lines are collapsed, thus preventing the ancestor list continuation from working as expected. Use this feature of the syntax with caution. If possible, enclose the nested list in an open block, as described in the previous section."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null,
                "type": "warning"
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Here’s an example of a paragraph that’s attached to the parent list item after the nested list ends. The empty line above the list continuation indicates that the block should be attached to current list item in the parent list."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "listing",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "* parent list item\n** child list item\n\n+\nparagraph attached to parent list item"
                  }
                ],
                "language": "asciidoc",
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Here’s how the source is rendered:"
                  }
                ],
